{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And they did so.</b> The word בלטיהם is from the root of ותבא אליו בלט (Judges 4:21), meaning secret things hidden from the eye. And the word is not deficient of he, for he is not a letter of continuation in the middle of a word. One may ask: if through Aaron all the waters of Egypt turned to blood, where did the magicians find water and turn it? The answer: Aaron turned only the waters that were on the earth, not the waters that were under the earth, and the magicians dug and drew out water and showed that it turned to blood. And there is a great difference between Aaron's deed and theirs, for Aaron turned the entire river that was before him, and all the waters in all the border of Egypt that he did not see; and furthermore, he turned waters that do not stand still but flow constantly, and other waters come; and furthermore, the plague lasted seven days, whereas the magicians showed that they turned only a little water standing in a vessel, and this was but a single moment, until Pharaoh returned to his house."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:28.478787195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}